.TH AVR\-JOB\-LOGS 1 "" "avr 0.1.3" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-job-logs \- View logs for a job, grouped by step.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr job logs
[OPTIONS] JOB_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
View logs for a job, grouped by step.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr job logs job-abc123
    avr job logs job-abc123 --failed
    avr job logs job-abc123 --step "Build" --level error
    avr job logs job-abc123 --follow
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIJOB_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-failed\fR
Only show logs from failed steps.
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter to a specific step by name.
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by log level. (choices: debug, info, notice, warning, error)
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\fR, \fB\-f\fR
Follow logs for in-progress jobs.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR
Include diagnostic-level lines (hidden by default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print directly to stdout instead of paging through `less`. Same as setting AVR_PAGER=''.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-job (1),
.BR avr-job-list (1),
.BR avr-job-metrics (1),
.BR avr-job-ssh (1),
.BR avr-job-view (1),
.BR avr-job-watch (1)
